 ### [Infinite Tiling with Modulo](1632-infinite-tiling-with-modulo.md)
-Infinite Tiling with Modulo is a technique for rendering infinite, repeating patterns by folding space using the modulo operator, allowing a single primitive Signed Distance Function (SDF) to be tiled infinitely. It enables ray-marched fractal renderers (e.g., Mandelbulbs, Menger sponges) that would be impossible to represent as explicit meshes. Unlike [Constructive SDF Modeling (Min Combination)](871-constructive-sdf-modeling-min-combination.md) which combines distinct primitives, this method transforms the query coordinate space to create periodicity.
